      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبَّيْتُهُ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَأْبِيَةٌ</span>, <i>I said to him</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِأَبِى</span> [meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُدِيَتِ بِأَبِى</span> <i>Mayest thou be ransomed with my
father!</i> or the like: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبٌ</span>, below]. (K, TA.
[In the CK, erroneously, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يا اَبِى</span>.])

